WEBVTT

00:01.210 --> 00:02.590
<i>I knew this race would be tough,</i>

00:02.750 --> 00:05.260
<i>but I didn't expect
anything like this.</i>

00:05.550 --> 00:07.800
<i>Our crash in the first race
of the preselections</i>

00:07.970 --> 00:09.800
<i>left us without a pilot.</i>

00:11.300 --> 00:12.300
<i>Or so I thought.</i>

00:16.560 --> 00:18.890
No, Jordan,
we can still win this race.

00:30.030 --> 00:32.450
<i>It was a miracle
we won the rematch.</i>

00:33.950 --> 00:36.120
<i>But our performance
didn't convince Don Wei,</i>

00:36.290 --> 00:37.870
<i>the Earth team manager.</i>

00:38.210 --> 00:40.790
<i>I don't know what the deal is
between Don Wei and Molly,</i>

00:40.960 --> 00:44.550
<i>but they seem to have
a real communication problem.</i>

02:12.090 --> 02:13.090
Mr. President,

02:13.260 --> 02:16.350
we have made it through
the first round of the preselections.

02:16.640 --> 02:18.220
But it was sheer luck.

02:18.390 --> 02:21.310
The irresponsible gamble
of a reckless girl.

02:22.520 --> 02:24.140
It's a painful
decision to make,

02:24.310 --> 02:26.230
but without Rick,
we have no other choice

02:26.400 --> 02:28.070
but to withdraw
from the competition.

02:28.440 --> 02:29.360
That's impossible.

02:30.110 --> 02:32.360
Mr. President,
she's just a young girl.

02:32.530 --> 02:34.950
She's not a pilot.
I cannot condone this.

02:35.490 --> 02:39.240
You should know that withdrawing
from the competition at this stage

02:39.410 --> 02:42.290
could bring about the total
destruction of the Earth Coalition,

02:42.450 --> 02:45.370
the end for more
than 16 billion people.

02:47.080 --> 02:48.920
You never explained

02:49.130 --> 02:52.420
that the situation
was so desperate.

02:52.840 --> 02:54.590
That's classified information.

02:54.760 --> 02:56.680
I told you
what you needed to know

02:56.840 --> 02:58.510
when you needed to know it.

02:58.680 --> 03:00.350
Today I can tell you this.

03:00.510 --> 03:02.770
The outcome
of the Great Race of Oban

03:02.930 --> 03:04.140
will radically transform

03:04.310 --> 03:06.400
the balance of power
within our galaxy.

03:07.770 --> 03:11.860
Therefore you must lead
the team as far as possible.

03:12.030 --> 03:12.940
Is that clear?

03:39.720 --> 03:40.890
Molly.

03:51.150 --> 03:53.070
Up early, I see.

03:53.530 --> 03:55.190
Where is your teammate hiding?

03:55.650 --> 03:57.320
You mean Molly?

03:57.780 --> 03:59.740
I have no idea.
She just ran off.

04:00.200 --> 04:01.660
She must be found immediately.

04:02.910 --> 04:06.910
We have a race
to prepare for, do we not?

04:09.420 --> 04:10.920
Are you serious?

04:11.080 --> 04:12.420
Thank you very much.

04:12.590 --> 04:14.000
Here, I'll find her right away.

04:44.330 --> 04:46.410
Another grenadine milk, pronto!

04:47.410 --> 04:48.830
Maybe you should stop.

04:49.000 --> 04:51.330
You know what they say.
Don't drink milk and drive.

04:51.830 --> 04:54.250
Listen, pal.
I already got a father.

05:34.750 --> 05:36.840
Look who's here.
Our little Eva.

05:39.630 --> 05:41.130
How are you, honey?

05:43.720 --> 05:47.140
Welcome to the Stern
Boarding School, my dear.

05:51.850 --> 05:52.850
Daddy!

05:56.570 --> 05:59.480
You must promise me
to be a good girl, Eva.

06:00.240 --> 06:03.320
Daddy's too busy
to take care of you now.

06:03.530 --> 06:04.950
Surely you can understand.

06:06.740 --> 06:08.160
-Daddy!
-Come along now.

06:12.910 --> 06:16.040
Please don't leave me, too, Daddy.

06:59.590 --> 07:00.960
Hey, Grooor.

07:01.130 --> 07:03.970
At least no one can say
you lack courage.

07:04.720 --> 07:08.800
I mean, after being humiliated
by those kids.

07:09.850 --> 07:14.310
Any other racer would have hidden
in a very deep hole.

07:16.730 --> 07:19.770
If ever I dig a very deep hole,

07:19.940 --> 07:22.690
it will be for your carcass!

07:38.380 --> 07:40.540
You know why I'm here.

07:40.960 --> 07:43.130
Uh, you've come
to congratulate me?

07:43.460 --> 07:44.550
Guess again.

07:45.090 --> 07:46.470
Well, you could have won,
you know.

07:46.630 --> 07:49.050
You didn't have to give me
that 30 second lead.

07:50.220 --> 07:52.310
Grooor has never lost a race.

07:52.850 --> 07:56.100
He is a fighter,
a champion among champions.

07:56.430 --> 08:00.230
You have robbed Grooor
of his victory.

08:01.230 --> 08:02.270
That's real funny.

08:02.440 --> 08:04.030
That's what my father said.

08:04.190 --> 08:05.610
You two should meet.

08:10.700 --> 08:14.330
Defend yourself
or kiss your life goodbye.

08:16.410 --> 08:18.370
Defend yourself, you big jerk.

08:24.420 --> 08:25.340
Excuse me.

08:25.510 --> 08:26.550
Excuse me, please.

08:28.050 --> 08:29.260
Molly!

08:31.220 --> 08:33.810
So, Mr. Grooor is
a sore loser, is that it?

08:51.700 --> 08:53.280
Not good.

08:53.660 --> 08:55.240
Are you all right?

08:55.540 --> 08:57.370
Mommy?
Is that really you?

08:57.790 --> 09:00.330
Come on, Jordan. Get up.
We've got to go now!

09:02.040 --> 09:04.040
Is that the best you can do?

09:07.630 --> 09:08.420
Don't.

09:17.810 --> 09:19.140
Grooor!

09:33.820 --> 09:34.820
Prince Aikka!

09:35.280 --> 09:37.620
Ah, well.
I guess my job's done.

09:39.080 --> 09:41.120
Out of my way, Nourasian.

09:41.370 --> 09:42.790
This is not your fight.

09:44.460 --> 09:47.710
But it is now, as you have chosen
a lesser creature to fight with.

09:50.300 --> 09:52.220
You are half Grooor's size.

09:52.550 --> 09:55.050
And soon I will
reduce you to nothing!

09:57.760 --> 09:58.770
Half the size...

10:00.680 --> 10:02.190
But twice the speed.

10:16.320 --> 10:18.120
Will you concede defeat?

10:42.480 --> 10:43.890
Thank you, very much.

10:44.730 --> 10:46.270
The pleasure was all mine.

10:48.150 --> 10:50.730
OK, show's over, Molly.
Let's go back.

10:50.900 --> 10:53.740
I don't want to hang out forever
with the lapdog of the Crogs.

10:53.900 --> 10:54.650
Jordan!

10:54.860 --> 10:57.200
The Nourasians are
no one's lapdog.

10:58.370 --> 10:59.620
Cut it out.

11:06.330 --> 11:07.920
Prince Aikka, wait!

11:10.880 --> 11:12.800
Jordan, have you gone off
the deep end?

11:12.960 --> 11:15.840
All right, maybe I was
a little rough on His Highness.

11:16.010 --> 11:16.930
He'll get over it.

11:17.140 --> 11:19.300
Prince Aikka just saved
your skinny neck.

11:19.470 --> 11:21.390
Well, no one asked him to.

11:23.180 --> 11:25.850
-At least Don Wei will be happy.
-What are you talking about?

11:26.020 --> 11:28.270
He wants you to be
the pilot of the Arrow 2.

11:28.610 --> 11:29.860
What?

11:30.520 --> 11:31.860
That's not funny, Jordan.

11:32.570 --> 11:34.650
It's the truth.
He told me to find you.

11:35.280 --> 11:36.990
That's impossible.

11:37.700 --> 11:39.570
I'm so angry with him.

11:48.080 --> 11:50.500
Come on!
We're gonna miss the race!

12:00.890 --> 12:01.890
You are late.

12:02.060 --> 12:03.310
Very late, Molly.

12:03.470 --> 12:06.310
You were so eager to race before.
Have you changed your mind?

12:06.560 --> 12:08.650
No, sir.
What made you change yours?

12:10.360 --> 12:12.650
That, young lady,
is none of your concern.

12:12.860 --> 12:14.440
Sir, please excuse Molly.

12:14.610 --> 12:17.650
It's been a rough morning.
She's not quite herself today.

12:17.820 --> 12:20.780
Jordan, there are times to talk
and times to be silent.

12:20.950 --> 12:22.620
Guess which one this is.

12:23.160 --> 12:26.330
Both of you,
get in the Arrow 2 immediately!

12:30.630 --> 12:33.540
Tell me, Molly,
do you get along well with your dad?

12:34.130 --> 12:35.050
Huh?

12:36.710 --> 12:37.880
What about my dad?

12:38.260 --> 12:42.220
I just hope your relationship with him
is better than you and Don Wei.

12:42.390 --> 12:43.930
My father is a great man.

12:44.390 --> 12:45.470
He adores me.

12:45.680 --> 12:48.560
Yeah. I get it.
The little princess looking for her...

12:48.730 --> 12:49.730
Buckle up!

12:55.570 --> 12:57.400
This is insane.

13:02.740 --> 13:06.620
We continue the second round
of preselections with the Earth team.

13:17.590 --> 13:18.720
And now,

13:19.090 --> 13:22.470
the one you've all been waiting for...

13:30.100 --> 13:33.150
The champion of Alwas,
our beloved planet.

13:33.520 --> 13:35.230
The great, the powerful...

13:35.610 --> 13:37.610
The mighty Flint!

13:40.860 --> 13:42.450
Flint! Flint!

13:43.410 --> 13:47.080
Accompanied
by his faithful companion, Marcel.

13:48.490 --> 13:49.660
Marcel!

13:50.120 --> 13:52.040
This is gonna be easy.

13:52.710 --> 13:54.040
Marcel! Marcel!

13:54.500 --> 13:57.050
This race will include a special rule.

13:58.960 --> 14:01.340
It's a trap circuit rule.

14:28.160 --> 14:30.330
Here's a love letter from Marcel!

14:35.880 --> 14:36.880
No way!

14:37.670 --> 14:39.170
Get a load of this!

14:53.390 --> 14:55.900
Hey, where did the little guy
go to, huh? To bed?

14:57.770 --> 15:00.610
-Marcel, we need more heat!
-Gotcha.

15:03.190 --> 15:04.700
Feast, my little darlings.

15:04.860 --> 15:06.280
Eat as much as you like.

15:24.470 --> 15:26.630
You know, Jordan,
I'm starting to get the hang of this.

15:28.050 --> 15:29.680
That remains to be seen.

15:32.930 --> 15:35.100
Any idea what
this trap circuit rule is?

15:40.230 --> 15:41.320
Give it a good tug.

15:45.110 --> 15:46.240
Dead ahead, Molly!

15:54.910 --> 15:57.170
-Missed!
-We'll get her next time around.

16:03.460 --> 16:04.670
Hey. why did it stop?

16:05.050 --> 16:06.420
How about this one?

16:06.590 --> 16:08.680
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's a good one.

16:25.490 --> 16:26.650
Oh, drat.

16:43.540 --> 16:45.090
Molly! Listen to me.

16:45.300 --> 16:46.550
The race is fixed.

16:46.920 --> 16:48.010
Ha! No kidding.

16:48.170 --> 16:51.680
Your only chance is to run
your adversary off the track.

16:57.600 --> 16:58.600
Marcel!

17:04.190 --> 17:05.610
My babies!

17:06.530 --> 17:07.780
How could you?

17:17.370 --> 17:19.040
This is not going to work.

17:21.460 --> 17:22.040
Molly!

17:22.210 --> 17:24.090
-Jordan, hold your fire.
-Are you nuts?

17:24.590 --> 17:27.130
Damage control, hull below 60%.

17:27.550 --> 17:29.170
Molly! What are you doing?

17:30.220 --> 17:32.590
You'd better quit
while you still can, little one.

17:32.800 --> 17:36.010
You don't stand a single chance
against the mighty Flint.

17:36.310 --> 17:38.980
You're mighty, all right.
A mighty cheat.

17:40.100 --> 17:42.230
All the traps are
against us and not you.

17:42.400 --> 17:43.900
You should be ashamed.

17:44.190 --> 17:46.440
It's not my fault if I'm lucky.

17:46.610 --> 17:48.650
Besides, with my amazing
natural talent,

17:48.820 --> 17:51.400
I could fly through these traps
with my eyes closed.

17:51.950 --> 17:53.820
OK, champ.
This one's all yours.

17:53.990 --> 17:55.660
I'll close my eyes.

18:00.790 --> 18:03.460
Just watch me and learn.

18:07.090 --> 18:08.550
Flint has lost his mind.

18:08.800 --> 18:10.130
We must stop it.

18:21.230 --> 18:22.520
Man, this guy's crazy.

18:24.190 --> 18:25.520
What did I tell you?

18:25.690 --> 18:28.610
Never underestimate
the mighty Flint.

18:28.860 --> 18:31.440
Not bad.
I guess you're just plain lucky.

18:32.030 --> 18:34.030
Plain lucky, you say?

18:34.200 --> 18:35.950
Watch this!

18:36.740 --> 18:37.990
Stop! Stop it quickly!

18:41.660 --> 18:42.910
That's the wrong technique.

18:43.080 --> 18:44.620
I know what I'm doing.

18:44.790 --> 18:47.040
-It's my job.
-Who says it's your...

18:50.210 --> 18:51.420
I laugh at this trap.

19:04.640 --> 19:06.810
Give me that.
We must increase the pace.

19:07.060 --> 19:08.310
Faster! Faster!

19:24.710 --> 19:27.170
No one can beat
the mighty Flint.

19:27.500 --> 19:30.920
I'm invincible!

20:03.950 --> 20:05.370
Marcel!

20:06.000 --> 20:07.160
It can't be!

20:16.170 --> 20:17.840
Yes? What now?

20:20.850 --> 20:24.640
The restoration of the great
Alwas empire will be delayed.

20:24.850 --> 20:26.600
It was a worthy attempt.

20:26.770 --> 20:28.390
And we can still
get a good deal

20:28.560 --> 20:29.810
selling the ship for scrap.

20:35.690 --> 20:38.610
I apologize for not being
at my best, sir.

20:38.950 --> 20:41.240
And sorry about the scratches
on the Arrow 2.

20:44.410 --> 20:46.700
Never mind.
It was a great race.

20:48.460 --> 20:50.710
Why don't you two
take the evening off?

20:50.880 --> 20:52.210
You deserve it.

20:54.670 --> 20:56.340
Who the heck was that guy?

20:56.510 --> 20:57.840
Don Wei's friendly clone?

21:01.260 --> 21:02.640
That was Don Wei, alright.

21:02.800 --> 21:04.600
Back to his old self again.

21:06.600 --> 21:07.390
What?

21:25.370 --> 21:27.080
Good to have you back, Rick.
